WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
Okay, this is where AI gets fun.

2
00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:05.390
Thirty-seven agents, six departments,

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.130
and a job for every one of them.

4
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.190
Let me show you.

5
00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:12.257
Click on an agent and you can see the
plan.

6
00:00:12.707 --> 00:00:16.557
Here's its job, here are the steps, and
here's what it needs to get going.

7
00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:18.223
And right in the middle?

8
00:00:18.313 --> 00:00:19.803
The company knowledge base.

9
00:00:20.333 --> 00:00:24.423
One place for the documents and
information the whole team needs.

10
00:00:24.993 --> 00:00:26.603
Everybody's on the same page.

11
00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:31.523
You've got communications, sales,
finance, client services, marketing,

12
00:00:31.813 --> 00:00:32.283
and tech.

13
00:00:32.913 --> 00:00:35.903
Each team has its own agents and
connected tools.

14
00:00:36.493 --> 00:00:38.383
Let's see what one actually does.

15
00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:40.297
This one's on cleanup duty.

16
00:00:40.847 --> 00:00:45.297
It's set up to check company documents
for old information and broken links.

17
00:00:45.847 --> 00:00:49.917
The steps, the agent, and its
instructions are all right here.

18
00:00:50.467 --> 00:00:51.177
Love that.

19
00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:52.987
And you still call the shots.

20
00:00:53.277 --> 00:00:55.827
Pick what you handle yourself, what
needs a review,

21
00:00:56.077 --> 00:00:58.047
and what you're comfortable letting run
automatically.

22
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:00.980
And you don't have to start from
scratch.

23
00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:06.280
There are starter setups for agencies,
consultants, and content studios.

24
00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:09.380
Pick the one that fits, then make it
yours.

25
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:10.870
Content calendar?

26
00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.420
Right here.

27
00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:16.320
What's drafted, what needs your okay,
and what's ready to go.

28
00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.580
So much easier to keep track.

29
00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:23.453
Over here, we can follow a lead from
that first hello to

30
00:01:23.453 --> 00:01:26.503
a proposal, all the way to a new client.

31
00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.123
Yes, please.

32
00:01:28.733 --> 00:01:30.223
And here's the money view.

33
00:01:30.433 --> 00:01:32.633
Invoices, payments, expenses.

34
00:01:32.633 --> 00:01:36.843
All together, so you can see what's
coming in and what's going out.

35
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.610
Finally, the coordinator brings it all
together for review.

36
00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.730
A team of agents, clear jobs, and you
keeping the final say.

37
00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:47.410
Pretty cool, right?

38
00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.120
Ready for your own AI team?

39
00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:54.760
Join me in the AI agents course, and
let's build it together!

40
00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.570
Want it done for your business instead?

41
00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:58.950
I can help with that, too.

42
00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.550
Register for the course, or reach out.

43
00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.950
Let's put AI to work!
